      <h1 id="virt-storage-checkups" class="group scroll-mt-20">Storage checkups<a href="#virt-storage-checkups" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">You can use a storage checkup to verify that the cluster storage is optimally configured for OpenShift Virtualization.</p>
      <p>Running a predefined checkup in an existing namespace involves setting up a service account for the checkup, creating the <code>Role</code> and <code>RoleBinding</code> objects for the service account, enabling permissions for the checkup, and creating the input config map and the checkup job. You can run a checkup multiple times.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You must always:</p>
          <ul>
          <li>Verify that the checkup image is from a trustworthy source before applying it.</li>
          <li>Review the checkup permissions before creating the <code>Role</code> and <code>RoleBinding</code> objects.</li>
          </ul>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <h2 id="virt-retain-storage-checkup-resources_virt-storage-checkups" class="group scroll-mt-20">Retaining resources for troubleshooting storage checkups<a href="#virt-retain-storage-checkup-resources_virt-storage-checkups" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">The predefined storage checkup includes <code>skipTeardown</code> configuration options, which control resource clean up after a storage checkup runs. By default, the <code>skipTeardown</code> field value is <code>Never</code>, which means that the checkup always performs teardown steps and deletes all resources after the checkup runs.</p>
      <p>You can retain resources for further inspection in case a failure occurs by setting the <code>skipTeardown</code> field to <code>onfailure</code>.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Run the following command to edit the <code>storage-checkup-config</code> config map:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc edit configmap storage-checkup-config -n <checkup_namespace>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Configure the <code>skipTeardown</code> field to use the <code>onfailure</code> value. You can do this by modifying the <code>storage-checkup-config</code> config map, stored in the <code>storage_checkup.yaml</code> file:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup-config\n  namespace: <checkup_namespace>\ndata:\n  spec.param.skipTeardown: onfailure\n# ..."} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Reapply the <code>storage-checkup-config</code> config map by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f storage_checkup.yaml -n <checkup_namespace>"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="virt-storage-checkup-web-console_virt-storage-checkups" class="group scroll-mt-20">Running a storage checkup by using the web console<a href="#virt-storage-checkup-web-console_virt-storage-checkups" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can run a storage checkup to validate that storage is working correctly for virtual machines.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>Navigate to <strong>Virtualization</strong> → <strong>Checkups</strong> in the web console.</li>
      <li>Click the <strong>Storage</strong> tab.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Install permissions</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Run checkup</strong>.</li>
      <li>Enter a name for the checkup in the <strong>Name</strong> field.</li>
      <li>Enter a timeout value for the checkup in the <strong>Timeout (minutes)</strong> fields.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Run</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Result</strong></p>
      <p>You can view the status of the storage checkup in the <strong>Checkups</strong> list on the <strong>Storage</strong> tab. Click on the name of the checkup for more details.</p>
      <h2 id="virt-checking-storage-configuration_virt-storage-checkups" class="group scroll-mt-20">Running a storage checkup by using the CLI<a href="#virt-checking-storage-configuration_virt-storage-checkups" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Use a predefined checkup to verify that the OpenShift Container Platform cluster storage is configured optimally to run OpenShift Virtualization workloads.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>
      The cluster administrator has created the required <code>cluster-reader</code> permissions for the storage checkup service account and namespace, such as in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: ClusterRoleBinding\nmetadata:\n  name: kubevirt-storage-checkup-clustereader\nroleRef:\n  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io\n  kind: ClusterRole\n  name: cluster-reader\nsubjects:\n- kind: ServiceAccount\n  name: storage-checkup-sa\n  namespace: <target_namespace> "} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;target_namespace&gt;</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the namespace where the checkup is to be run.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a <code>ServiceAccount</code>, <code>Role</code>, and <code>RoleBinding</code> manifest file for the storage checkup.
      <p>Example service account, role, and rolebinding manifest:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ServiceAccount\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup-sa\n---\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: Role\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup-role\nrules:\n  - apiGroups: [ \"\" ]\n    resources: [ \"configmaps\" ]\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"update\"]\n  - apiGroups: [ \"kubevirt.io\" ]\n    resources: [ \"virtualmachines\" ]\n    verbs: [ \"create\", \"delete\" ]\n  - apiGroups: [ \"kubevirt.io\" ]\n    resources: [ \"virtualmachineinstances\" ]\n    verbs: [ \"get\" ]\n  - apiGroups: [ \"subresources.kubevirt.io\" ]\n    resources: [ \"virtualmachineinstances/addvolume\", \"virtualmachineinstances/removevolume\" ]\n    verbs: [ \"update\" ]\n  - apiGroups: [ \"kubevirt.io\" ]\n    resources: [ \"virtualmachineinstancemigrations\" ]\n    verbs: [ \"create\" ]\n  - apiGroups: [ \"cdi.kubevirt.io\" ]\n    resources: [ \"datavolumes\" ]\n    verbs: [ \"create\", \"delete\" ]\n  - apiGroups: [ \"\" ]\n    resources: [ \"persistentvolumeclaims\" ]\n    verbs: [ \"delete\" ]\n---\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\nkind: RoleBinding\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup-role\nsubjects:\n  - kind: ServiceAccount\n    name: storage-checkup-sa\nroleRef:\n  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io\n  kind: Role\n  name: storage-checkup-role"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply the <code>ServiceAccount</code>, <code>Role</code>, and <code>RoleBinding</code> manifest in the target namespace:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -n <target_namespace> -f <storage_sa_roles_rolebinding>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a <code>ConfigMap</code> and <code>Job</code> manifest file. The config map contains the input parameters for the checkup job.
      <p>Example input config map and job manifest:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"---\napiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup-config\n  namespace: $CHECKUP_NAMESPACE\ndata:\n  spec.timeout: 10m\n  spec.param.storageClass: ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd-virtualization\n  spec.param.vmiTimeout: 3m\n---\napiVersion: batch/v1\nkind: Job\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup\n  namespace: $CHECKUP_NAMESPACE\nspec:\n  backoffLimit: 0\n  template:\n    spec:\n      serviceAccount: storage-checkup-sa\n      restartPolicy: Never\n      containers:\n        - name: storage-checkup\n          image: quay.io/kiagnose/kubevirt-storage-checkup:main\n          imagePullPolicy: Always\n          env:\n            - name: CONFIGMAP_NAMESPACE\n              value: $CHECKUP_NAMESPACE\n            - name: CONFIGMAP_NAME\n              value: storage-checkup-config"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply the <code>ConfigMap</code> and <code>Job</code> manifest file in the target namespace to run the checkup:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -n <target_namespace> -f <storage_configmap_job>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Wait for the job to complete:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc wait job storage-checkup -n <target_namespace> --for condition=complete --timeout 10m"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Review the results of the checkup by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get configmap storage-checkup-config -n <target_namespace> -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Example output config map (success):</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup-config\n  labels:\n    kiagnose/checkup-type: kubevirt-storage\ndata:\n  spec.timeout: 10m\n  status.succeeded: \"true\" \n  status.failureReason: \"\" \n  status.startTimestamp: \"2023-07-31T13:14:38Z\" \n  status.completionTimestamp: \"2023-07-31T13:19:41Z\" \n  status.result.cnvVersion: 4.21.2 \n  status.result.defaultStorageClass: trident-nfs\n  status.result.goldenImagesNoDataSource: <data_import_cron_list> \n  status.result.goldenImagesNotUpToDate: <data_import_cron_list> \n  status.result.ocpVersion: 4.21.0\n  status.result.pvcBound: \"true\"\n  status.result.storageProfileMissingVolumeSnapshotClass: <storage_class_list> \n  status.result.storageProfilesWithEmptyClaimPropertySets: <storage_profile_list> \n  status.result.storageProfilesWithSmartClone: <storage_profile_list>\n  status.result.storageProfilesWithSpecClaimPropertySets: <storage_profile_list>\n  status.result.storageProfilesWithRWX: |-\n    ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd\n    ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd-virtualization\n    ocs-storagecluster-cephfs\n    trident-iscsi\n    trident-minio\n    trident-nfs\n    windows-vms\n  status.result.vmBootFromGoldenImage: VMI \"vmi-under-test-dhkb8\" successfully booted\n  status.result.vmHotplugVolume: |-\n    VMI \"vmi-under-test-dhkb8\" hotplug volume ready\n    VMI \"vmi-under-test-dhkb8\" hotplug volume removed\n  status.result.vmLiveMigration: VMI \"vmi-under-test-dhkb8\" migration completed\n  status.result.vmVolumeClone: 'DV cloneType: \"csi-clone\"'\n  status.result.vmsWithNonVirtRbdStorageClass: <vm_list>\n  status.result.vmsWithUnsetEfsStorageClass: <vm_list>"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <ul>
      <li><code>data.status.succeeded</code> defines if the checkup is successful (<code>true</code>) or not (<code>false</code>).</li>
      <li><code>data.status.failureReason</code> defines the reason for failure if the checkup fails.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.startTimestamp</code> defines the time when the checkup started, in RFC 3339 time format.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.completionTimestamp</code> defines the time when the checkup has completed, in RFC 3339 time format.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.cnvVersion</code> defines the OpenShift Virtualization version.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.defaultStorageClass</code> defines if there is a default storage class.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.goldenImagesNoDataSource</code> defines the list of golden images whose data source is not ready.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.goldenImagesNotUpToDate</code> defines the list of golden images whose data import cron is not up-to-date.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.ocpVersion</code> defines the OpenShift Container Platform version.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.pvcBound</code> defines if a PVC of 10Mi has been created and bound by the provisioner.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.storageProfileMissingVolumeSnapshotClass</code> defines the list of storage profiles using snapshot-based clone but missing VolumeSnapshotClass.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.storageProfilesWithEmptyClaimPropertySets</code> defines the list of storage profiles with unknown provisioners.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.storageProfilesWithSmartClone</code> defines the list of storage profiles with smart clone support (CSI/snapshot).</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.storageProfilesWithSpecClaimPropertySets</code> defines the list of storage profiles spec-overriden claimPropertySets.</li>
      <li><code>data.status.result.vmsWithNonVirtRbdStorageClass</code> defines the list of virtual machines that use the Ceph RBD storage class when the virtualization storage class exists.</li>
      <li>
      <code>data.status.result.vmsWithUnsetEfsStorageClass</code> defines the list of virtual machines that use an Elastic File Store (EFS) storage class where the GID and UID are not set in the storage class.
      <ol>
      <li>
      Delete the job and config map that you previously created by running the following commands:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete job -n <target_namespace> storage-checkup"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete config-map -n <target_namespace> storage-checkup-config"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Optional: If you do not plan to run another checkup, delete the <code>ServiceAccount</code>, <code>Role</code>, and <code>RoleBinding</code> manifest:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete -f <storage_sa_roles_rolebinding>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="virt-troubleshoot-storage-checkup_virt-storage-checkups" class="group scroll-mt-20">Troubleshooting a failed storage checkup<a href="#virt-troubleshoot-storage-checkup_virt-storage-checkups" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">If a storage checkup fails, there are steps that you can take to identify the reason for failure.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You have downloaded the directory provided by the <code>must-gather</code> tool.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Review the <code>status.failureReason</code> field in the <code>storage-checkup-config</code> config map by running the following command and observing the output:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get configmap storage-checkup-config -n <namespace> -o yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Example output config map:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: storage-checkup-config\n  labels:\n    kiagnose/checkup-type: kubevirt-storage\ndata:\n  spec.timeout: 10m\n  status.succeeded: \"false\"\n  status.failureReason: \"ErrNoDefaultStorageClass\"\n# ..."} lang="yaml" />
      <ul>
      <li>If the checkup has failed, the <code>status.succeeded</code> value is <code>false</code>.</li>
      <li>If the checkup has failed, the <code>status.failureReason</code> field contains an error message. In this example output, the <code>ErrNoDefaultStorageClass</code> error message means that no default storage class is configured.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li>Search the directory provided by the <code>must-gather</code> tool for logs, events, or terms related to the error in the <code>data.status.failureReason</code> field value.</li>
      </ol>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/virt/support/virt-collecting-virt-data#virt-collecting-virt-data">Collecting data for Red Hat Support</a></li>
      <li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/virt/support/virt-collecting-virt-data#virt-using-virt-must-gather_virt-collecting-virt-data">Using the <code>must-gather</code> tool for OpenShift Virtualization</a></li>
      </ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="virt-troubleshoot-storage-checkup-error-codes_virt-storage-checkups" class="group scroll-mt-20">Storage checkup error codes<a href="#virt-troubleshoot-storage-checkup-error-codes_virt-storage-checkups" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Storage checkup error codes might appear in the <code>storage-checkup-config</code> config map after a storage checkup fails.</p>
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Error code</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Meaning</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrNoDefaultStorageClass</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>No default storage class is configured.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrPvcNotBound</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>One or more persistent volume claims (PVCs) failed to bind.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrMultipleDefaultStorageClasses</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>Multiple default storage classes are configured.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrEmptyClaimPropertySets</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>There are <code>StorageProfile</code> objects containing empty <code>ClaimPropertySets</code> specs.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrVMsWithUnsetEfsStorageClass</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>There are VMs using elastic file system (EFS) storage classes, where the GID and UID are not set in the <code>StorageClass</code> object.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrGoldenImagesNotUpToDate</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>One or more golden images has a <code>DataImportCron</code> object that is either not up to date or has a <code>DataSource</code> object which is not ready.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrGoldenImageNoDataSource</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>The <code>DataSource</code> object of the golden image has either no PVC or no snapshot source configured.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>ErrBootFailedOnSomeVMs</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>Some VMs failed to boot within the expected time.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
    </article>
